SUMMARY:Yom Ha'atzmaut Nature Festival: Celebrating Israel's 78th Independence Day at Pearlstone
DESCRIPTION:יום העצמאות ה-78 למדינת ישראל \nCampus Location: The Myerberg Stage at the Greenwald Amphitheater \n\n\n \nCelebrate Israel’s 78th Independence Day\nJoin Pearlstone’s Shaliach\, Avihay\, along with the Baltimore-based Shinshinim of the Jewish Agency for Israel and enjoy this time to connect to our roots through nature\, food\, Israeli sounds\, and to unite in prayer and hope for peace. \nRegisterEvent Details🕓 Schedule:\n• 4:00–5:00 PM — Zip line\n• 5:00–8:00 PM — Mesibah (party) with activity stations \n🎉 Activities:\nTreasure hunt · Family zip line · Nature walk to the Nachal (creek hike) · Pitas on the saj · Fresh Israeli salad & hummus from the Pearlstone kitchen · Israeli jewelry-making · Face painting · Israeli dancing & music · Trivia with prizes · Israeli DJ \n🎒 Please bring: comfortable clothes for outdoor activities · water bottle · hat \n🎈 This is a child and family-friendly event! Share special moments with your children and pass on the love of our heritage to them. \n✡️ As we gather at this meaningful junction of national days — Passover\, Yom HaShoah\, Yom HaZikaron\, and Yom Ha’atzmaut — we find strength in coming together. Join us in this circle of connection\, joy\, and tradition.
URL:https://adamah.org/event/pearlstone-yom-haatzmaut-nature-festival/
LOCATION:Pearlstone Retreat Center & Campus\, 5425 Mt. Gilead Rd\, Reisterstown\, MD\, 21136
CATEGORIES:Pearlstone
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://adamah.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Yom-Haatzmaut-e1774369368487.jpg
END:VEVENT
