SUMMARY:Mother’s Day R&R Weekend at Pearlstone
DESCRIPTION:Good kids take their moms to brunch on Mother’s Day\, GREAT kids take her to Pearlstone! \nTreat your mom to a full weekend of nurturing R&R at Pearlstone this Mother’s Day – delicious farm-to-table meals\, a joyous Shabbat\, light family programming in nature on our gorgeous 180-acre farm\, comfortable accommodations\, yoga\, eco-spa\, games\, and lots of memories!  Includes Pearlstone’s famous Sunday brunch!  (Brunch only option also available.) \n\nRegisterEvent Details \n\n		Sample Schedule\n		 \nFriday \n\n\n\n4-6pm\nCheck-in & Welcome Snack\nMain Lobby\n\n\n5-6pm\nA Gift for Mom:  Eco Spa or Jewelry Making\nVineyard\n\n\n6:30pm\n Women’s Prayer Circle\nTree of Life\n\n\n7pm\nEarly Shabbat Candle-lighting \nTree of Life\n\n\n\nMincha/Maariv (pending minyan)\nJubilee\n\n\n7:45pm\nShabbat Dinner \nOrchard\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \nSaturday\n \n\n\n\n8:00 am\nFeed the Sheep with Avihay\nPasture\n\n\n8-9:30 am\nBreakfast\nOrchard\n\n\n8:00 am\nGame Room Open All Day (children 10 and under must be supervised by an adult)\nEarth\n\n\n9 am\nDavening & Torah Reading (pending minyan)\nJubilee\n\n\n10:30am\nMommy & Me Yoga for All Ages\nBeit Midrash\n\n\n12-2pm\nShabbat Lunch\nOrchard\n\n\n2-3 pm\nPrayer Walk & Farm Tour\nMain Lobby\n\n\n3:15-4:15 pm\n“Honor Your Mother:” Memories & Storytelling\nBeit Midrash\n\n\n4-5pm\nSnack\nMain Lobby\n\n\n7 pm\nShalosh Seudot (3rd Meal) \nDining Room\n\n\n\nMincha/Maariv (pending minyan)\nJubilee\n\n\n8:58 pm\nHavdalah\nOrchard/Vineyard\n\n\n9:15 pm\nCampfire & Smores\nPasture Fire Pit\n\n\n\nSunday \n\n\n\n9:00-11am\nPearlstone’s Famous Brunch \nOrchard/Dining Room\n\n\n\n9:15 am\nMorning Movement (Women & Girls Only)\nBeit Midrash\n\n\n\n11:00 am\nCheck Out Procedure: \nComplete Survey & Drop Room Key in Basket\nMain Lobby\n\n\n\n\n\n\nNOTE: THERE WILL BE NO KIDS CAMP and parents are expected to supervise their children at all times.\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n		Dining\n		 \n\nWe are proud of our kosher farm-to-table kitchen under the supervision of the Orthodox Union (OU).\nWe strive to follow Adamah’s mission of cultivating a more sustainable future by centering our food offerings around lots of vegetarian options\, what is presently available on our farm and what we can source locally. Our delicious meals reflect the season and land at the time of your visit.\nAll meals will be buffet style and have open seating\nAs we are not licensed to serve alcohol\, guests are welcome to bring any kind of wine/alcohol as long as it is sealed\, heckschered as MEVUSHAL\, and checked by our mashgiach at the registration desk upon arrival.\n\n\n	\n\n		Davening & Jewish Ritual Elements\n		 \nWe will offer community-led Shabbat services with a mehitzah Friday night and Saturday day if there is enough interest to make a minyan. \nWe will have all the customary elements of Shabbat including candle-lighting\, challah\, grape juice\, havdalah – and even matzah ball soup! \nWe have a natural creek mikvah and an eruv around the entire property including hiking trails. \n\n	\n\n		 Attire\n		 \n\n\nOur Mother’s Day R&R Weekend will be retreat-center-casual. Remember layers\, sneakers and yoga clothes!\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n		 FAQs\n		 \nPearlstone Guest Experience & FAQ
URL:https://adamah.org/event/mothers-day-rr-weekend-at-pearlstone/
LOCATION:Pearlstone Retreat Center & Campus\, 5425 Mt. Gilead Rd\, Reisterstown\, MD\, 21136
CATEGORIES:Pearlstone,Retreats
